      "body": "Fixes #27231.\n\n## Summary\n- keep the request-level `background` flag when `GenerateReqInput.__getitem__` slices an `n > 1` batch into per-sample requests\n- add a regression test so Responses API background jobs do not silently fall back to foreground disconnect handling after slicing\n\n## To verify\n- `python -m py_compile python\\sglang\\srt\\managers\\io_struct.py test\\registered\\unit\\managers\\test_io_struct.py`\n- `python -m ruff check python\\sglang\\srt\\managers\\io_struct.py test\\registered\\unit\\managers\\test_io_struct.py`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nI also attempted the targeted pytest on Windows:\n\n`PYTHONPATH=python python -m pytest test\\registered\\unit\\managers\\test_io_struct.py::TestGenerateReqInputNormalization::test_getitem_preserves_background -q`\n\nThat collection is blocked locally by Linux/GPU-oriented imports (`resource`, then `triton`).\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37001383098](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001383098)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37001383432](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001383432)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37001383025](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37001383025)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Scope note for the Gemini review: this PR intentionally fixes only the background flag loss from #27231.\n\nThe other fields mentioned by the bot are covered separately so that each PR stays reviewable:\n- require_reasoning and routing_key: #27199\n- multimodal controls and mm_hashes: #27259\n- session_params indexing: #27257\n\nKeeping background isolated also matches the issue impact: Responses API background jobs can be aborted incorrectly when __getitem__ resets background to false.",
            "createdAt": "2026-06-04T12:08:55Z",
            "databaseId": 4621983399,
            "updatedAt": "2026-06-04T12:08:55Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/27255#issuecomment-4621983399"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Re-surfacing this one after some time. The background flag is still dropped when a request gets sliced, and the fix here preserves it with a regression test. I cannot add the run-ci label myself, so if a maintainer thinks this is worth landing, adding the label is all it needs from me.",
            "createdAt": "2026-08-19T12:37:25Z",
            "databaseId": 5342196940,
            "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T12:37:25Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/27255#issuecomment-5342196940"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Re-checked against current main today: `GenerateReqInput.__getitem__` still reconstructs the sub-request without `background` (the field exists on the class; it is just not forwarded in the slice), so a batch with `background=True` silently turns into foreground sub-requests and the responses API never sees the flag. The one-line forward plus the batch regression test still apply cleanly. Happy to rebase if a maintainer confirms the slice should forward it.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-11T13:57:18Z",
            "databaseId": 5635497608,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-11T13:57:18Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/27255#issuecomment-5635497608"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "he-yufeng"
            },
            "body": "Re-verified on current main (93809202a3): `GenerateReqInput.__getitem__` still rebuilds the per-sample request field by field and `background` is still not among the copied fields, so an `n > 1` background batch still falls back to foreground disconnect handling on slice (#27231). Four months in the queue; could a maintainer add the run-ci label? The fix is one field plus a regression test.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-12T22:22:01Z",
