  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile propagating the `background` flag in `GenerateReqInput.__getitem__`, we should also propagate other request-level fields that are currently missing, such as `require_reasoning`, `use_audio_in_video`, and `routing_key`. This prevents these flags from being lost when a batch request is sliced into individual subrequests.\n\n```suggestion\n            background=self.background,\n            require_reasoning=self.require_reasoning,\n            use_audio_in_video=self.use_audio_in_video,\n            routing_key=self.routing_key,\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-06-04T08:26:39Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -716,6 +716,7 @@ def __getitem__(self, i):\n             return_bytes=self.return_bytes,\n             return_entropy=self.return_entropy,\n             return_prompt_token_ids=self.return_prompt_token_ids,\n+            background=self.background,",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/27255#discussion_r3354571110",
      "id": 3354571110,
      "line": 1024,
      "original_line": 719,
      "path": "python/sglang/srt/managers/io_struct.py",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-04T08:26:39Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "gemini-code-assist[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)\n\nExpand the test case to also verify that `require_reasoning`, `use_audio_in_video`, and `routing_key` are correctly preserved when slicing the batch request.\n\n```python\n    def test_getitem_preserves_background(self):\n        \"\"\"Batch subrequests must keep the background response flag and other request-level flags.\"\"\"\n        req = GenerateReqInput(\n            text=[\"Hello\", \"World\"],\n            sampling_params=[{}, {}],\n            rid=[\"id1\", \"id2\"],\n            background=True,\n            require_reasoning=True,\n            use_audio_in_video=True,\n            routing_key=\"test_key\",\n        )\n        req.normalize_batch_and_arguments()\n\n        self.assertTrue(req[0].background)\n        self.assertTrue(req[1].background)\n        self.assertTrue(req[0].require_reasoning)\n        self.assertTrue(req[1].require_reasoning)\n        self.assertTrue(req[0].use_audio_in_video)\n        self.assertTrue(req[1].use_audio_in_video)\n        self.assertEqual(req[0].routing_key, \"test_key\")\n        self.assertEqual(req[1].routing_key, \"test_key\")\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-06-04T08:26:39Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -552,6 +552,19 @@ def test_getitem_preserves_return_prompt_token_ids(self):\n         self.assertTrue(req[0].return_prompt_token_ids)\n         self.assertTrue(req[1].return_prompt_token_ids)\n \n+    def test_getitem_preserves_background(self):\n+        \"\"\"Batch subrequests must keep the background response flag.\"\"\"\n+        req = GenerateReqInput(\n+            text=[\"Hello\", \"World\"],\n+            sampling_params=[{}, {}],\n+            rid=[\"id1\", \"id2\"],\n+            background=True,\n+        )\n+        req.normalize_batch_and_arguments()\n+\n+        self.assertTrue(req[0].background)\n+        self.assertTrue(req[1].background)",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/27255#discussion_r3354571126",
